---js
// <script>
let headerTitle = "Build Awesome is a simpler website generator";
let layout = "layouts/docs.njk";

let searchTitle = "Build Awesome is a simpler website generator";

let eleventyNavigation = {
	parent: "Eleventy Documentation",
	key: "Home",
	pinned: true,
};

let eleventyImport = {
	collections: ["blog"]
};

let eleventyComputed = {
	social: {
		description: () => "Build Awesome (Eleventy) is a simpler website generator."
	},
};

let opengraphCard = true;
// </script>
---
<script webc:setup>
export function getHighlightedBlogPostContent(collection) {
	let posts = findBy(collection, 'data.blogHighlight', true);
	if(!posts.length) {
		return "";
	}
	posts.reverse();

	// Only the most recent few here; everything else is a link away in the archives.
	let shown = posts.slice(0, 6);

	let content = [];
	let index = 0;
	for(let post of shown) {
		content.push(`<li><a href="${post.url}">${index === 0 ? `<strong>` : ""}${post.data.newstitle}${index === 0 ? `</strong>` : ""}</a> (<em>${newsDate(post.date)}</em>)</li>`);
		index++;
	}
	// 10 hardcoded posts on the blog
	content.push(`<li>…and <a href="/blog/">${collection.length + 10 - shown.length} more on the <strong>blog archives</strong></a>.</li>`)

	return `${content.join("")}`;
}
</script>

<p>Build Awesome is a developer tool to help you build <a href="/docs/performance/"><strong>fast websites</strong> even faster</a>.</p>

<ul>
	<li>It’s <strong>secure</strong> and <strong>resilient</strong>: static websites let you skip the runtime and keep your uptime.</li>
	<li>It’s <strong>lightweight</strong>: we’ve <a href="/blog/dependency-watch/">decreased our dependency count</a> with every major release since 2018.</li>
	<li>It’s <strong>scalable</strong>: deploy with the most efficient architecture for the modern agent-heavy web.</li>
	<li>It’s <strong>stable</strong>: stop getting burned upgrading your dependencies. We want your website to deploy <em>without headaches</em> for years to come.</li>
	<li>It’s <a href="/docs/why/"><strong>trusted</strong></a> by folks at <img webc:is="indieweb-avatar" url="https://www.nasa.gov/"><abbr title="National Aeronautics and Space Administration">NASA</abbr> <img webc:is="indieweb-avatar" url="https://home.web.cern.ch/">Cern <img webc:is="indieweb-avatar" url="https://tc39.es/">TC39 <img webc:is="indieweb-avatar" url="https://about.google/">Google <img webc:is="indieweb-avatar" url="https://www.microsoft.com/">Microsoft <img webc:is="indieweb-avatar" url="https://www.cloudflare.com/">Cloudflare <img webc:is="indieweb-avatar" url="https://www.mozilla.org/">Mozilla (and more).</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>You should have a website</strong> and Build Awesome can help you create your very own home on the web. <a href="/docs/">Get started!</a></p>

<template webc:type="11ty" 11ty:type="njk" webc:raw webc:nokeep>
{% include "pro-cta.njk" %}
</template>

<!--- <ul>
	<li>Build Awesome: runs on your computer.</li>
	<li>Build Awesome Pro: run on our computers. (coming soon!)</li>
</li> --->

<quick-start></quick-start>

<div webc:bucket="async" webc:nokeep>
	<h2>News from the Blog</h2>
	<ul @html="getHighlightedBlogPostContent(collections.blog)"></ul>

	<giant-docs-button></giant-docs-button>
	<giant-docs-button-subtext></giant-docs-button-subtext>

	<h2>Built Awesome</h2>

	<sites-list>
		<site-card :show-icons="true" size="opengraph" webc:for="(key, site) in shuffle($data.builtwith)" webc:if="!site.disabled && site.featured" :featured="site.featured" :url="site.demo || site.url" :iconUrl="site.iconUrl" :name="site.name" :date="false"></site-card>
	</sites-list>

	<is-land on:visible on:save-data="false">
		<facepile>
			<html-fetch src="/imports/facepile.html"></html-fetch>
		</facepile>
	</is-land>

	<p>A random sample taken from <a href="/authors/"><code><span @text="Object.keys($data.builtwithAuthors).length"></span></code> authors</a>. Check out the <a href="/speedlify/">fastest of their <code><span @text="getsize(objectFilterNot(builtwith, 'disabled'))" webc:nokeep></span></code> websites</a>.</p>

	<h2>Don’t take my word for it <emoji @char="🌈" @alt="Rainbow"></emoji></h2>

	<p>Listen to what these <a href="/docs/testimonials/">happy developers</a> are saying about Build Awesome and Eleventy:</p>

	<testimonials-list :@testimonials="testimonials"></testimonials-list>

	<p><a href="/docs/testimonials/">…and many more!</a></p>

	<h2>Alternatives</h2>

	<p>This project aims to directly compete with all other website generators. We encourage you to try out a few others:</p>

	<lists webc:nokeep>
		<ul class="inlinelist">
			<li><a href="https://jekyllrb.com/">Jekyll (Ruby)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://gohugo.io/">Hugo (Go)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://hexo.io/">Hexo (JavaScript)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://www.gatsbyjs.org/">Gatsby (JavaScript using React)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://nuxtjs.org/">Nuxt (JavaScript using Vue)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://nextjs.org/">Next.js (JavaScript using React)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://www.bridgetownrb.com/">Bridgetown (Ruby)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://astro.build/">Astro (JavaScript)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://remix.run/">Remix (JavaScript using React)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://kit.svelte.dev/">SvelteKit (JavaScript using Svelte)</a></li>
			<li><a href="https://jamstack.org/generators/"><em>More at jamstack.org</em></a></li>
		</ul>
	</lists>
</div>

